#️⃣ 1. University Scholarship Allocation


📝 Problem Statement

Build a program that checks scholarship applicants against aggregate marks, minimum marks in every required subject, attendance, and family-income limits. Eligible applicants are ranked, with ties resolved by predefined rules.

🎯 Objectives

• Validate applicant data and eligibility criteria.
• Compute aggregate percentage and apply all minimum thresholds.
• Rank eligible applicants using marks, attendance, then lower family income as tie-breakers.
• Display eligibility, rank, and reasons for rejection.

💡 Assumptions

• Marks are percentages from 0 to 100; subject marks are entered as a list.
• Eligibility requires aggregate \(\ge \) 80, every subject \(\ge \) 60, attendance \(\ge \) 75%, and annual family income \(\le \) 300,000.
• Tie-break order: higher aggregate, higher attendance, lower income, then earlier input order.
• The sample uses three subjects and a fixed scholarship quota of two.

🛠️ Algorithm & Logic

1. Read applicant count (\(n\)), name, three subject marks, attendance, and annual family income.
2. Calculate aggregate as the mean of the three subject marks.
3. Mark an applicant eligible only if all four threshold rules pass.
4. Store eligible records as tuples: (aggregate, attendance, -income, -input_order, name).
5. Sort eligible tuples in descending order.
6. Assign ranks and display up to the quota limit as scholarship recipients.

Flowchart


    Start([START]) --> InputCount[/Input Applicant Count/]
    InputCount --> LoopStart{For Each Applicant}
    
    LoopStart -->|Yes| InputDetails[/Input Name, Marks, Attendance, Income/]
    InputDetails --> CalcAvg[Calculate Aggregate Average]
    CalcAvg --> CheckRules{Avg >= 80 AND<br>All Marks >= 60 AND<br>Attendance >= 75% AND<br>Income <= 300000}
    
    CheckRules -->|True| StoreTuple[Store tuple with sort weights]
    CheckRules -->|False| PrintIneligible[/Print NOT ELIGIBLE/]
    
    StoreTuple --> LoopStart
    PrintIneligible --> LoopStart
    
    LoopStart -->|No More Applicants| SortRecords[Sort stored records in descending order]
    SortRecords --> DisplayRanked[/Display ranked list up to Quota limit/]
    DisplayRanked --> End([STOP])
Use code with caution.

💻 Python Implementation

python
n = int(input("Applicants: "))
a = []
for i in range(n):
    name = input("Name: ")
    m = [float(input("Subject mark: ")) for _ in range(3)]
    att = float(input("Attendance: "))
    inc = float(input("Income: "))
    avg = sum(m) / 3
    ok = avg >= 80 and min(m) >= 60 and att >= 75 and inc <= 300000
    a.append((avg, att, -inc, -i, name)) if ok else print(name, "NOT ELIGIBLE")

a.sort(reverse=True)
for i, x in enumerate(a):
    print(i + 1, x[4], round(x[0], 2), "AWARDED" if i < 2 else "")
Use code with caution.

