#️⃣ 2. Progressive Electricity Billing


📝 Problem Statement

Calculate monthly household electricity bills using progressive consumption slabs, fixed charges, surcharges, and rebates. Compare bills over consecutive months to flag unusual consumption increases.

🎯 Objectives

• Apply progressive slab rates sequentially across consumption limits.
• Add fixed operational costs, percentage surcharges, and discount rebates.
• Monitor month-over-month variances and flag dynamic spikes above a threshold.

💡 Assumptions

• Slabs: First 100 units at ₹2/unit, next 100 units at ₹3/unit, units above 200 at ₹5/unit.
• Charges: Fixed charge of ₹75; surcharge is 5% of energy charge.
• Rebate: Deduction of ₹50 if consumption is at most 100 units.
• An increase is marked unusual when a bill rises by >30% from the previous month.

🛠️ Algorithm & Logic

1. Read the number of total months (\(n\)) and each month's total energy unit consumption.
2. Calculate energy cost progressively across slabs using boundary capping values.
3. Apply fixed configurations, add a 5% surcharge, and subtract rebate allowances.
4. From the second tracked month onward, calculate percentage change relative to index i-1.

Flowchart

mermaid
graph TD
    Start([START]) --> InputMonths[/Input Total Months/]
    InputMonths --> LoopStart{For Each Month}
    
    LoopStart -->|Yes| InputUnits[/Input Consumed Units/]
    InputUnits --> CheckSlab1{Units <= 100}
    
    CheckSlab1 -->|Yes| Calc1[Energy = Units * 2]
    CheckSlab1 -->|No| CheckSlab2{Units <= 200}
    
    CheckSlab2 -->|Yes| Calc2[Energy = 100*2 + Units-100 * 3]
    CheckSlab2 -->|No| Calc3[Energy = 100*2 + 100*3 + Units-200 * 5]
    
    Calc1 --> MainBill[Base Bill = Energy + 75 + Energy * 0.05]
    Calc2 --> MainBill
    Calc3 --> MainBill
    
    MainBill --> RebateCheck{Units <= 100}
    RebateCheck -->|Yes| ApplyRebate[Bill = Bill - 50]
    RebateCheck -->|No| StoreBill[Store and Print Monthly Bill]
    ApplyRebate --> StoreBill
    
    StoreBill --> CheckSpike{Not Month 1 AND<br>Increase > 30%}
    CheckSpike -->|True| AlertSpike[/Print UNUSUAL INCREASE/]
    CheckSpike -->|False| LoopStart
    AlertSpike --> LoopStart
    
    LoopStart -->|No More Months| End([STOP])
Use code with caution.

💻 Python Implementation

python
n = int(input("Months: "))
bills = []
for i in range(n):
    u = float(input("Units: "))
    e = 2 * min(u, 100) + 3 * min(max(u - 100, 0), 100) + 5 * max(u - 200, 0)
    b = e + 75 + e * .05 - (50 if u <= 100 else 0)
    bills.append(b)
    print("Bill", i + 1, round(b, 2))
    if len(bills) > 1 and bills[-2] > 0 and (b - bills[-2]) / bills[-2] > .30:
        print("UNUSUAL INCREASE")
