#️⃣ 3. Hospital Billing and Patient Classification


📝 Problem Statement

Prepare patient statements combining consultation, diagnostic, and treatment charges. Apply dynamic concession rules, validate monetary limits, and classify payment statuses.

🎯 Objectives

• Structure dynamic itemized entry calculations.
• Formulate threshold concession deductions safely.
• Classify overall ledger flags as PAID, PARTIALLY PAID, or OUTSTANDING.

💡 Assumptions

• Concession is fixed at 10% when gross structural charges are \(\ge \) ₹5,000.
• Balance zero \(\rightarrow \) PAID.
• Payment greater than zero but less than bill \(\rightarrow \) PARTIALLY PAID.
• Payment equal to zero \(\rightarrow \) OUTSTANDING.

🛠️ Algorithm & Logic

1. Read patient name, consultation fee, diagnostic cost, and treatment expenses.
2. Enforce explicit validation that all input charges are non-negative (\(\ge \) 0).
3. Compute baseline subtotal, determine conditional threshold discounts, and process net totals.
4. Read actual paid amount; flag accounts out of range or process remaining statement balance.

