#️⃣ 6. Railway Fare and Reservation Calculator


📝 Problem Statement

Calculate dynamic rail travel fares across tier distances, travel classification modifiers, age-group concession rules, reservation overhead processing, and cancellation fine matrices.

🎯 Objectives

• Code staggered progressive lookup slabs for mileage cost baselines.
• Integrate multiplier factors based on cabin classification.
• Automate refund distributions or fine execution logic upon cancellation flags.

💡 Assumptions

• Distance Rate Slabs:
	• First 100 km \(\rightarrow \) ₹1.20/km
	• Next 400 km \(\rightarrow \) ₹1.00/km
	• Distance beyond 500 km \(\rightarrow \) ₹0.80/km
• Class Factors: Sleeper = 1.0, AC = 2.0, Chair Car = 1.4.
• Age Concessions: Under 12 receives 50% discount; seniors (\(60+\)) receive 30% discount.
• Reservation process costs ₹40; cancellations trigger a 25% base fare penalty, and reservation fees are non-refundable.

🛠️ Algorithm & Logic

1. Read itinerary distance and passenger count (\(n\)).
2. Determine continuous slab baseline travel cost.
3. For each traveler, process age bracket concessions and cabin modifiers.
4. If a cancellation flag is active, compute the penalty balance and issue the remaining refund.

