#️⃣ 7. Retail Billing with Multiple Discount Rules


📝 Problem Statement

Generate an itemized retail store invoice across multiple distinct item branches. Apply category-specific retail taxes, handle discount thresholds, and enforce a maximum concession limit.

🎯 Objectives

• Track inventory categories and aggregate taxes.
• Process percentage-based conditional invoice discounts.
• Enforce maximum concession caps.

💡 Assumptions

• Category Tax Rates: Grocery = 5%, Electronics = 18%, Clothing = 12%.
• Discounts: 10% subtotal deduction applies when pre-tax gross sums are \(\ge \) ₹5,000.
• Maximum discount reduction cap is strictly limited to ₹1,000.

🛠️ Algorithm & Logic

1. Read the number of total checkout products (\(n\)), item department classification, cost, and quantities.
2. Accumulate subtotal values and track pre-tax category entries.
3. If subtotal counts cross \(\ge \) ₹5,000, trigger a 10% discount check capped at the ₹1,000 limit.
4. Apply the discount proportionally across items, compute itemized tax totals, and print the summary invoice.

