#️⃣ 8. Manufacturing Cost and Profitability Analysis


📝 Problem Statement

Decompose industrial production finance metrics across baseline material yields, wastage thresholds, manual human labor assets, and operational machine overhead components. Measure final net margins against target thresholds.

🎯 Objectives

• Factor wastage tracking into raw material costs.
• Aggregate variable human resource hours with fixed mechanical expenses.
• Formulate comparative production return models.

💡 Assumptions

• Wastage expense is computed as a direct percentage of the baseline raw material subtotal.
• \(\text{Profit Margin} = \frac{\text{Net Profit}}{\text{Gross Revenue}} \times 100\).
• Target validation flags a success indicator when the actual margin satisfies the minimum required goal.

🛠️ Algorithm & Logic

1. Read quantity batch, raw product component needs, material price, wastage percentage, human working hours/rates, machinery operation fees, sales values, and target metrics.
2. Calculate base material costs and apply the wastage scalar addition.
3. Sum labor products with machinery values to calculate the total operating cost.
4. Compute revenue, net profit, and profit margin, then check if the target margin is achieved.

Flowchart

mermaid
graph TD
    Start([START]) --> InputManufacturing[/Input Quantity, Material Requirements, Rates, Wastage, Labor Hours, Labor Rates, Machine Expenses, Sale Price, Target Margin/]
    InputManufacturing --> CheckValid{Quantity <= 0 OR<br>Any Cost/Rate < 0}
    
    CheckValid -->|Yes| PrintError[/Display Invalid Input; STOP/]
    CheckValid -->|No| CalcCosts[Base Material = Quantity * Material Per Unit * Material Rate<br>Wastage Cost = Base Material * Wastage Percent / 100<br>Labor Total = Hours * Hourly Rate<br>Total Cost = Base Material + Wastage Cost + Labor Total + Machine Cost]
    
    CalcCosts --> CalcReturns[Gross Revenue = Quantity * Selling Price<br>Net Profit = Gross Revenue - Total Cost]
    CalcReturns --> CheckRev{Gross Revenue > 0}
    
    CheckRev -->|Yes| CalcMargin[Margin Percent = Net Profit / Gross Revenue * 100]
    CheckRev -->|No| ZeroMargin[Margin Percent = 0]
    
    CalcMargin --> EvaluateTarget{Margin Percent >= Target Margin}
    ZeroMargin --> EvaluateTarget
    
    EvaluateTarget -->|True| MetaTarget[Output Metrics Summary + TARGET MET]
    EvaluateTarget -->|False| MissTarget[Output Metrics Summary + TARGET NOT MET]
    
