#️⃣ 9. Multi-Currency Travel Budget Analysis


📝 Problem Statement

Convert multi-currency ledger rows into a standardized home currency using custom user-supplied exchange rates. Factor transactional banking fees into total expenses and track variance budgets alongside prominent expense classifications.

🎯 Objectives

• Convert multiple foreign exchange rates to a single base currency.
• Calculate conversion transaction processing fees.
• Aggregate expenses by category to find the largest spending source.

💡 Assumptions

• Rates track standard unit ratios from home currency per single foreign unit.
• Conversion fees are fixed at a 2% addition onto all raw calculated currency products.
• Datasets map storage models formatted as list arrays containing (category, cost).

🛠️ Algorithm & Logic

1. Read the global base currency allowance amount and itemized expense counts (\(n\)).
2. Loop through entries to read category string tags, origin codes, and current rate values.
3. Multiply values by exchange rates and apply the 1.02 fee scalar addition.
4. Consolidate category sums, track the largest spending source, and check the budget balance.

