#️⃣ 10. Campus Event Financial Planning


📝 Problem Statement

Estimate total organizational campus event funding across fixed venue/equipment resources and variable participant indices. Determine corporate registration fee margins, sponsorship shortfalls, and break-even points.

🎯 Objectives

• Aggregate structural corporate base parameters with dynamic head-count rates.
• Forecast cash flows and sponsorships shortfalls.
• Model break-even registration numbers using a mathematical ceiling logic loop.

💡 Assumptions

• Venue/equipment map to fixed matrices; catering, logistics transport, and certificates apply per-person.
• \(\text{Break-Even Point} = \lceil\frac{\text{Total Fixed Expenses} - \text{Sponsorship Funding}}{\text{Registration Unit Fee} - \text{Variable Unit Expense Per Head}}\rceil\).
• If unit registration fees \(\le \) variable per-head expenses, breaking even via ticket sales alone is impossible.

🛠️ Algorithm & Logic

1. Read venue and equipment costs, per-person rates (catering, transport, certificates), expected registrations, unit ticket price, and sponsorships.
2. Sum parameters into total operational costs and compare against target income projections.
3. Subtract the variable cost per participant from the unit registration fee to find the net contribution margin.
4. If net contribution margin is positive, apply ceiling metrics to determine the exact minimum registration threshold to prevent losses.

